{%- comment -%}
  One frame in the What's included image grid.

  Two sources can fill that grid: the section's own Image blocks, and a product
  metafield that overrides them for a single product. The frame markup lives
  here so both sources emit an identical figure, because the grid CSS keys off
  data-count and :nth-child and would drift the moment the two paths diverged.

  Parameters
    image - an image drop. A block's image_picker setting, or one file out of a
            file_reference list metafield.
    alt   - optional override. Falls back to the image's own alt text.
    attrs - block.shopify_attributes, so the theme editor can still select the
            block. Left empty for metafield images, which are not blocks.
    span  - true when this frame runs the full width of the gallery rather than
            sharing a row. The caller knows that from the image count: one image
            fills the gallery, and in a three-image grid the third spans both
            columns. Everything else is half a row.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # sizes has to describe the width the frame really renders at, or Shopify
  # picks a candidate off the widths list that is too small and the browser
  # scales it up. The old value described a half-row frame at every count, so
  # a spanning frame asked for 34vw and got roughly half the pixels it needed
  # - measured 490px of image in a 721px slot at 1440, and 377px in 793px at
  # 820, which is where the softness came from.
  #
  # Measured frame widths, gallery / half-row:
  #   1440+  721 / 354      1200  596 / 292      1024  537 / 262
  #   900    873 / 431       820  793 / 391       750  723 / 356
  # Below 750 the grid becomes a carousel and every frame is the full width.
  if span
    assign incl_img_sizes = '(min-width: 1440px) 730px, (min-width: 990px) 56vw, 100vw'
  else
    assign incl_img_sizes = '(min-width: 1440px) 360px, (min-width: 990px) 28vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw'
  endif
-%}

{%- if image != blank -%}
  {%- assign incl_img_alt = alt | default: image.alt -%}
  <figure class="ori-gvm-incl__frame" data-gallery-slide {{ attrs }}>
    {{-
      image
      | image_url: width: 1200
      | image_tag:
        loading: 'lazy',
        class: 'ori-gvm-incl__img',
        widths: '360,540,720,960,1200',
        sizes: incl_img_sizes,
        alt: incl_img_alt
    -}}
  </figure>
{%- endif -%}
